{"t":1785930161261,"type":"FeatureCollection","features":[{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.06a3dc8a6faacbf0430ab2e127360ea830dbc45d.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-150.8,61.77],[-151.15,61.92],[-151.08,61.99],[-150.88,62.01],[-150.67,61.86],[-150.8,61.77]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.06a3dc8a6faacbf0430ab2e127360ea830dbc45d.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.06a3dc8a6faacbf0430ab2e127360ea830dbc45d.001.1","areaDesc":"Western Susitna Valley","geocode":{"SAME":["002170"],"UGC":["AKZ745"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/AKZ745"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c4f2259a84ad44e4728e395ff49d445ac176fe71.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c4f2259a84ad44e4728e395ff49d445ac176fe71.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-04T08:14:00-08:00"}],"sent":"2026-08-04T15:54:00-08:00","effective":"2026-08-04T15:54:00-08:00","onset":"2026-08-04T15:54:00-08:00","expires":"2026-08-07T13:00:00-08:00","ends":"2026-08-07T13:00:00-08:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Anchorage AK","headline":"Flood Warning issued August 4 at 3:54PM AKDT until August 7 at 1:00PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...Yentna River including Lake Creek.\n\n* WHEN...Until 100 PM AKDT Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Streams\ncontinue to rise due to excess runoff from earlier rainfall.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 348 PM AKDT, The river gauge at the Yentna River at Lake\nCreek indicates rises in water levels from heavy rain across\nthe warned area. Flooding is ongoing. Trees and debris larger\nthan telephone poles have been observed flowing down the\nriver. Between 1.0 and 2.5 inches of rain have fallen.\nAdditional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch are possible\nwith higher amounts possible in the upper Yentna Basin.\n- For Yentna River at Lake Creek:\nAt 7:51am the stage was 20.7 feet.\nFlood Stage is 20.5 feet.\nForecast: A crest slightly above 22 feet late tonight and\ninto early Wednesday morning.\n\nImpacts:\nBetween 21 and 22 feet, several lodges may have water in or\naround low-lying cabins.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Stay tuned to further developments by listening to your local radio,\ntelevision, or NOAA Weather Radio for further information.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSAFC"],"WMOidentifier":["WGAK88 PAFC 042354"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 1 PM AKDT FRIDAY"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.PAFC.FA.W.0005.000000T0000Z-260807T2100Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-07T13:00:00-08:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FLS"],"NationalWeatherService":["FAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.15496853d81a7696b9600e483af722795486a1d2.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-150.76,62.57],[-150.48,62.55],[-150.48,62.38],[-150.52,62.32],[-150.56,62.28],[-150.62,62.21],[-150.7,62.18],[-150.77,62.22],[-150.83,62.31],[-150.98,62.38],[-151.08,62.45],[-151.05,62.53],[-150.76,62.57]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.15496853d81a7696b9600e483af722795486a1d2.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.15496853d81a7696b9600e483af722795486a1d2.001.1","areaDesc":"Central Susitna Valley","geocode":{"SAME":["002170"],"UGC":["AKZ747"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/AKZ747"],"references":[],"sent":"2026-08-04T08:45:00-08:00","effective":"2026-08-04T08:45:00-08:00","onset":"2026-08-04T08:45:00-08:00","expires":"2026-08-05T17:00:00-08:00","ends":"2026-08-05T17:00:00-08:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Expected","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Anchorage AK","headline":"Flood Warning issued August 4 at 8:45AM AKDT until August 5 at 5:00PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Petersville Area\n\n* WHEN...Until 500 PM AKDT Wednesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Low-water\ncrossings are inundated with water and may not be passable.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 842 AM AKDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges\nindicated heavy rain across the warned area. Flooding is\nongoing or expected to begin shortly. Between 2 and 3 inches\nof rain have fallen. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to\n1.5 inches are possible.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Stay tuned to further developments by listening to your local radio,\ntelevision, or NOAA Weather Radio for further information.\n\nTurn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nIn hilly terrain there are hundreds of low water crossings which are\npotentially dangerous in heavy rain. Do not attempt to cross flooded\nroads. Find an alternate route.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLWAFC"],"WMOidentifier":["WGAK48 PAFC 041645"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING IN EFFECT UNTIL 5 PM AKDT WEDNESDAY"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.PAFC.FA.W.0006.260804T1645Z-260806T0100Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-05T17:00:00-08:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FLW"],"NationalWeatherService":["FAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6d551781f3f6acf01a2f1dc9da49c5479d73b83d.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-93.59,40.35],[-93.53,40.58],[-93.38,40.58],[-93.37,40.29],[-93.59,40.35]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6d551781f3f6acf01a2f1dc9da49c5479d73b83d.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6d551781f3f6acf01a2f1dc9da49c5479d73b83d.001.1","areaDesc":"Mercer, MO","geocode":{"SAME":["029129"],"UGC":["MOC129"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/MOC129"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.039863342af3389063e3662241d2eaea2898fc29.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.039863342af3389063e3662241d2eaea2898fc29.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-05T05:54:00-05:00"},{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3a93f3780ac3d991c1eb7b7fff2e643cca69a1df.002.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3a93f3780ac3d991c1eb7b7fff2e643cca69a1df.002.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-05T06:16:00-05:00"}],"sent":"2026-08-05T06:28:00-05:00","effective":"2026-08-05T06:28:00-05:00","onset":"2026-08-05T06:28:00-05:00","expires":"2026-08-05T06:45:00-05:00","ends":"2026-08-05T06:45:00-05:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Kansas City/Pleasant Hill MO","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 5 at 6:28AM CDT until August 5 at 6:45AM CDT by NWS Kansas City/Pleasant Hill MO","description":"At 628 AM CDT, a severe thunderstorm was located 13 miles east of\nMercer, or 15 miles west of Unionville, moving east at 50 mph.\n\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts 