sageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Kansas City/Pleasant Hill MO","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 5 at 6:20AM CDT until August 5 at 7:00AM CDT by NWS Kansas City/Pleasant Hill MO","description":"SVREAX\n\nThe National Weather Service in Pleasant Hill has issued a\n\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...\nNorthern Sullivan County in north central Missouri...\nPutnam County in north central Missouri...\n\n* Until 700 AM CDT.\n\n* At 619 AM CDT, a severe thunderstorm was located near Mercer, or 21\nmiles south of Corydon, moving east at 50 mph.\n\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and quarter size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect wind damage\nto roofs, siding, and trees.\n\n* Locations impacted include...\nUnionville, Green City, Greencastle, Newtown, Pollock, Lucerne,\nHarris, Powersville, Lemons, and Green Castle.","instruction":"For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a\nbuilding.","response":"Shelter","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["SVREAX"],"WMOidentifier":["WUUS53 KEAX 051120"],"eventMotionDescription":["2026-08-05T11:19:00-00:00...storm...278DEG...43KT...40.46,-93.43"],"windThreat":["RADAR INDICATED"],"maxWindGust":["60 MPH"],"hailThreat":["RADAR INDICATED"],"maxHailSize":["1.00"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.KEAX.SV.W.0441.260805T1120Z-260805T1200Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-05T07:00:00-05:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["SVR"],"NationalWeatherService":["SVW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cfe0cb53516243e5682c1b93f097af5f347ba9d1.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-98.33,28.43],[-98.08,28.5],[-97.86,28.15],[-97.94,28.1],[-98.15,28.36],[-98.33,28.33],[-98.33,28.43]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cfe0cb53516243e5682c1b93f097af5f347ba9d1.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cfe0cb53516243e5682c1b93f097af5f347ba9d1.001.1","areaDesc":"Live Oak, TX","geocode":{"SAME":["048297"],"UGC":["TXC297"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/TXC297"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.52c53adf21b8a3c6773f1bc49de7351006f6e777.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.52c53adf21b8a3c6773f1bc49de7351006f6e777.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-04T08:54:00-05:00"},{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0d85f3f3b48cc9017f55a16e1f1acf4cc74e9f0b.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0d85f3f3b48cc9017f55a16e1f1acf4cc74e9f0b.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-04T15:51:00-05:00"}],"sent":"2026-08-04T20:07:00-05:00","effective":"2026-08-04T20:07:00-05:00","onset":"2026-08-04T20:07:00-05:00","expires":"2026-08-05T11:15:00-05:00","ends":"2026-08-06T20:10:00-05:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Corpus Christi TX","headline":"Flood Warning issued August 4 at 8:07PM CDT until August 6 at 8:10PM CDT by NWS Corpus Christi TX","description":"...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in Texas...\n\nNueces River Near Three Rivers affecting Live Oak County.\n\nNueces River Near Tilden affecting McMullen County.\n\nFor the Nueces River...including Cotulla, Tilden, Three Rivers,\nMathis, Bluntzer, Calallen...Moderate flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Moderate flooding is occurring and moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHERE...Nueces River near Three Rivers.\n\n* WHEN...Until Thursday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 32.0 feet, The Nueces River backs up minor creeks to\nnear the slab elevation of homes in the River Creek Acres\nSubdivision, five miles southeast of George West. Livestock are cut\noff and could drown in low areas of the flood plain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 7:15 PM CDT Tuesday the stage was 33.5 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 20.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage early\nThursday morning and continue falling to 9.0 feet Sunday evening.\n- Flood stage is 25.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nEven 6 inches of fast-moving flood water can knock you off your feet\nand a depth of 2 feet will float your car. Never try to walk, swim,\nor drive through such swift water. If you come upon flood waters,\nstop, turn around and go another way.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/crp.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSCRP"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS84 KCRP 050107"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL THURSDAY EVENING"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KCRP.FL.W.0027.000000T0000Z-260807T0110Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-06T20:10:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1890e16dec93bc7bd2c40c556f7d88b51dfba240.001.1,2026-08-03T20:13:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6c2d46f696ba508a8268a87165a57be61f4e50bb.001.1,2026-08-03T09:17:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a89341f8395f18ac2219ce1a412989c19cd5d270.001.1,2026-08-02T20:24:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.135a0f1988967bd17c986e8c8d19aa89231c27b7.001.1,2026-08-02T14:39:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0