ps and tank batteries occurs. Fences and hunting\ncabins are damaged.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 7:30 PM CDT Tuesday the stage was 17.2 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 11.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage\nThursday evening and continue falling through the weekend.\n- Flood stage is 14.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nEven 6 inches of fast-moving flood water can knock you off your feet\nand a depth of 2 feet will float your car. Never try to walk, swim,\nor drive through such swift water. If you come upon flood waters,\nstop, turn around and go another way.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/crp.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSCRP"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS84 KCRP 050107"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL FRIDAY MORNING"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KCRP.FL.W.0026.000000T0000Z-260807T1643Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-07T11:43:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1890e16dec93bc7bd2c40c556f7d88b51dfba240.002.1,2026-08-03T20:13:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6c2d46f696ba508a8268a87165a57be61f4e50bb.002.1,2026-08-03T09:17:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a89341f8395f18ac2219ce1a412989c19cd5d270.002.1,2026-08-02T20:24:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.135a0f1988967bd17c986e8c8d19aa89231c27b7.002.1,2026-08-02T14:39:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1b543241930cc661baf187477778f4d98e6501dc.001.1,2026-08-02T08:25:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b4d720713368e37fddd68843d1aab38758412622.0